    {
      "id": "r20261119-a02",
      "title": "Learning a Language with Music",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "Many students find grammar books boring, so they try a more fun method: songs. Teachers say music can be a powerful tool for learning a language, and science agrees.",
        "Songs help in several ways. A good melody makes words easier to remember - that is why you still remember songs from your childhood. Singing also trains your mouth to make new sounds, and listening teaches you how native speakers connect words together.",
        "Of course, songs cannot teach you everything. Lyrics are sometimes strange or ungrammatical because the words must fit the music. The best plan is to mix: use songs for vocabulary and pronunciation, and books or classes for grammar. Then your English will improve, and you will enjoy the journey."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "boring": "membosankan",
        "method": "metode",
        "powerful tool": "alat yang ampuh",
        "melody": "melodi",
        "childhood": "masa kecil",
        "lyrics": "lirik",
        "ungrammatical": "tidak gramatikal",
        "improve": "meningkat"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "Why do songs make words easier to remember?",
          "opts": [
            "Songs are always short",
            "Lyrics are always simple",
            "A good melody helps memory"
          ],
          "a": 2
        },
        {
          "q": "What is one weakness of learning from songs?",
          "opts": [
